{"title":"2015 CIMC Problems/Part A Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the diagram, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is a square with side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> are the midpoints of the sides of the square, as shown. What is the area of the shaded region?\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_2&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The area of the shaded region is the area of the unshaded triangles subtracted from the area of the square. The side length of the square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so the area of the square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/e/d0e9136809f832318fdd66a5180d0e20660e072b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4^{2} = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> are the midpoint of the sides of the square, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/1/961007924073f7cbcf66888f8e375320e13f8d65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BP = BQ = DR = DS = \\frac{4}{2} = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"260\" height=\"38\" />. This means that the area of each triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c68db3e0d509ed2818b814745df993312893847c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2 \\times 2}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"46\" height=\"38\" />, so the area of the two triangles is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/a/4aae69d5a3cf3e7239ddd216b41562e0c55d903f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 2 = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>The area of the shaded region is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/8/398b3f725fee794d01b082695df25cb1fd4e37a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16 - 4 = \\boxed{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"103\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The shaded region can be split up like this, forming two triangles and a rectangle:\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_2&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> are the midpoint of the sides of the square, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/1/961007924073f7cbcf66888f8e375320e13f8d65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BP = BQ = DR = DS = \\frac{4}{2} = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"260\" height=\"38\" />. This means that the area of each triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c68db3e0d509ed2818b814745df993312893847c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2 \\times 2}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"46\" height=\"38\" />, so the area of the two triangles is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/a/4aae69d5a3cf3e7239ddd216b41562e0c55d903f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 2 = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>From the isosceles right triangles, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/e/55e9919dfa0cf095c8247de6ec6c3b1de70e0c54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PS = QR = RS = PQ = 2\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"242\" height=\"23\" />, so the area of the rectangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/f/67fac9cc3fbf08c28c11ffcb50f27d0ca9a2e706.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2\\sqrt{2})^{2} = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"90\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p><p>The area of the shaded region is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/4/bb4a1c36dab332a9d89e13a24c2303aaeaae239b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8 + 4 = \\boxed{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"96\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CIMC\" title=\"2015 CIMC\">2015 CIMC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CIMC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2015 CIMC Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CIMC_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2015 CIMC Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_1\" title=\"2015 CIMC Problems/Part A Problem 1\">Part A Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2015 CIMC Problems/Part A Problem 3 (page does not exist)\">Part A Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_1\" title=\"2015 CIMC Problems/Part A Problem 1\">Part A 1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Part A 2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2015 CIMC Problems/Part A Problem 3 (page does not exist)\">Part A 3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_4\" title=\"2015 CIMC Problems/Part A Problem 4\">Part A 4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_5\" title=\"2015 CIMC Problems/Part A Problem 5\">Part A 5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2015 CIMC Problems/Part A Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">Part A 6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CIMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2015 CIMC Problems/Part B Problem 1 (page does not exist)\">Part B 1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CIMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2015 CIMC Problems/Part B Problem 2 (page does not exist)\">Part B 2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CIMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2015 CIMC Problems/Part B Problem 3 (page does not exist)\">Part B 3</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=CEMC_Intermediate_Competition\" title=\"CEMC Intermediate Competition\">CEMC Intermediate Competition</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018060729\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.029 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.049 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 183/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1974/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 140/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4679/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   16.555      1 -total\n 48.08%    7.959      1 Template:CEMC_CIMC/CSMC_box\n 37.71%    6.243      2 Template:Image_needed\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:37173:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018060729 and revision id 287072. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}